 that mostly sit on the contact

Fan used any-point containment, so a contact patch touched by a perimeter loop turned the fan override on for the whole wall: on the goose project 92989 outer-wall and 51217 inner-wall moves printed inside the fan zone. Speed and flow already used the majority rule; the fan now uses it too, and the object-on-interface joint no longer applies to support paths (its subject is the object material resting on the interface; the support side keeps its contact settings). In-zone object moves drop from 152036 to 1240. The test now slices TestMesh::overhang, whose flat underside puts paths mostly inside the contact.
